    "prompt_en": "Inside a partially flooded Baroque archive, the scene centers an unmistakably adult woman conservation scientist aligning a vellum leaf beneath a raised glass platen as a chandelier-like pulley drying rack turns under a dripping painted dome. A restrained frontal waist-up portrait ensures the full hairline temple cheek jaw and chin perimeter remains visible, with hair pinned away from temples, cheek edges, jaw corners, and chin; natural adult facial texture and mature proportions remain clear. The designed diamond zygomatic-dominant face contour is explicit: the face length-to-width relation remains readable; cheekbone width exceeds forehead and jaw widths; the contour narrows toward both forehead and small chin; front-view width remains separate from depth lighting and styling. Her expression is neutral. Soft bilateral face-shaping light and low-distortion portrait perspective keep both facial sides legible while one gloved hand works the vellum and the other steadies a humidity sensor. Gilded shelves, suspended catalog ribbons, reflected candles, shallow water, ornate stucco, and conservation tools form layered architectural depth behind her.",
